Third-party material and references
-----------------------------------

IEEE OUI registry
  server/lib/network/oui.tsv is a reduced copy of the public MA-L listing of the IEEE
  Registration Authority (https://standards-oui.ieee.org/oui/oui.csv), regenerated by
  server/scripts/update-oui.js. It maps MAC address prefixes to vendor names.

Icons
  No icon is shipped in this repository. scripts/vendor-icons.mjs downloads, on demand, the icons
  named in the configuration from:
    - dashboard-icons (https://github.com/homarr-labs/dashboard-icons), Apache License 2.0;
    - selfh.st icons (https://github.com/selfhst/icons), Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
      International (CC BY 4.0).
  The source of every downloaded file is recorded in ICONS_DIR/sources.json.

Service definitions
  The format and approach of server/lib/network/service-defs.json are inspired by Scanopy
  (AGPL-3.0). No code was copied.

Service widgets
  The generic widget engine (fields read from a JSON path or a Prometheus metric and formatted on the
  server) and the Open-Meteo weather widget follow ideas from Homepage
  (https://github.com/gethomepage/homepage, GPL-3.0). No code was copied.

Weather data
  The optional weather widget queries Open-Meteo (https://open-meteo.com) at runtime. Open-Meteo
  data is provided under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International license (CC BY 4.0).

ARP companion image
  docker/net-scan/Dockerfile installs arp-scan (GPL-3.0-or-later) from the Debian packages. The
  companion image is built locally and is not distributed; a distributed image must provide the
  corresponding source code.

Dependencies
  The npm dependencies of client/ and server/ keep their own licenses (see their package-lock.json
  files and each package's license file).
